.TH KARASHEKA 6 "2026-11-23" "karasheka 1.0.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
karasheka \- retro 2D karate game in a furnished apartment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B karasheka
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Karasheka
is a retro karate game in which two karateka fight it out in an apartment:
the living room, the kitchen, the bedroom and the study.
Jump onto the furniture to get out of the way, then dive kick down on your
opponent; light furniture breaks under a heavy landing.
.PP
Play against the computer (Easy, Normal or Hard), against a second player on
the same keyboard, or watch two computers fight.
All graphics and sound are generated by the game while it runs.
.SH CONTROLS
Each fighter uses nine direction keys laid out like a numeric keypad, plus a
strike key and a guard key.
Playing alone, any of the layouts can be used, and mixed.
.TS
l l l l.
Layout	Directions	Strike	Guard
Left hand	Q W E / A S D / Z X C	Left Shift	Left Ctrl
Right hand	Y U I / H J K / N M ,	Space	L
Numpad	7 8 9 / 4 5 6 / 1 2 3	Right Shift or Num 0	Right Ctrl or Num Enter
.TE
.PP
On their own the directions jump (top row), walk (middle row) and roll or
crouch (bottom row); the middle key guards mid.
With strike they attack; with guard, up guards high, nothing guards mid and
down guards low.
Each attack is blocked only by the guard at its height.
.PP
.TS
l l.
Esc	pause
F1	show all the keys
F2	sound on or off
F11, Alt+Enter	fullscreen
.TE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-size " W" x H
Window (or capture) size.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " file.bmp"
Play a computer fight offscreen, save one frame and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-scene " name"
What to capture: menu, intro, fight, ko, over, help, pause, cover or poses.
.TP
.BI \-\-time " seconds"
Fight time before a capture.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " n"
Match seed for captures and recordings.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " file"
Play the showcase clip and write raw RGB24 frames to
.I file
(\- for standard output).
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " n"
Frame rate for
.BR \-\-record .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Karasheka/Karasheka/settings.ini
The menu choices.
